# install.sh is fetched and piped straight into bash. Checked out with CRLF it
# fails on the shebang - "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" - naming a
# program that is plainly installed.
*.sh  text eol=lf

# The Windows installer is the opposite: a .cmd with LF endings misbehaves in
# cmd.exe. `text eol=crlf` is NOT enough here, and that is the whole point of
# this comment: it converts on checkout, but raw.githubusercontent.com serves
# the normalised blob straight out of the index, so a downloaded file is always
# LF no matter what the attribute says.
#
# `-text` disables normalisation entirely. The bytes committed are the bytes
# served, so the CRLF has to be right in the working tree at commit time.
*.cmd -text
